{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>On the other side of the Jordan, Moses began to explain this Torah.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Moses wished to explain to them now, in the fortieth year, all the commandments and the essence of this Torah, which is the Ten Commandments; and since the fathers had heard them from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, Moses went back and caused the sons to hear them, and they heard them from his mouth. And even though they already knew this from the mouths of their fathers and believed in them, behold, the prophecy of Moses is clear to them and firmly established in their eyes, and what they hear from his mouth is as if they heard it from the mouth of the Most High." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: ״בארץ מואב הואיל משה באר את התורה הזאת לאמר״ — the Torah is expounded in forty-nine faces of purity and in forty-nine faces of impurity, like the numeration of מואב; and thus it is written (Song of Songs 5:10): ״דודי צח ואדום״, which is to say, twenty-four books are expounded forty-nine to the right and to the left — this is דודי צח ואדום; and this is what is written (Proverbs 2:4): ״וכמטמונים תחפשנה״ — forty-nine countings, from the language of (Genesis 31): ״עשרת מונים״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The gematria of מואב = 49; דודי = 24 (the 24 books of Scripture); the verse from Song of Songs 5:10 is read as an allusion to 24 (= דודי) and 49 (from צח ואדום read as 49 by the same method). Rabbeinu Bahya leaves the numerology implicit, as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:31.807786139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}